@prefix cd: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/> .
@prefix ex: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/specifications/level6-statistical-tests> {
  ex:l6-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Statistical Tests"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-motivation-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Is this difference more than measurement variation?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-motivation a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-motivation-a, ex:l6-motivation-b, ex:l6-motivation-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-motivation-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "DOES THE METHOD READ TOO LOW?"@en ; cd:body "- QC target: **50 µg/L**\n- Mean of repeated preparations: **48.5 µg/L**\n- Random variation or a systematic departure?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-motivation-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "DOES THE RIVER CONCENTRATION CHANGE?"@en ; cd:body "- Measure **diclofenac** in river water\n- **Before / after the industrial park:** upstream / downstream\n- Is the mean concentration higher downstream?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-motivation-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "DOES EXPOSURE CHANGE ALGAL GROWTH?"@en ; cd:body "- Control and diclofenac-exposed cultures\n- Estimate one growth rate per independent culture\n- Do the **mean growth rates** differ?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-hypotheses-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Every test starts with a hypothesis"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-hypotheses a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-hypotheses-a, ex:l6-hypotheses-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-hypotheses-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "H₀: ALWAYS INCLUDES EQUALITY HERE"@en ; cd:body "- In these classical comparisons: **=, ≤ or ≥**\n- New limit example: **amoxicillin**, mean **at or below** the limit\n- Predict how the test statistic varies under H₀."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-hypotheses-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "H₁: NEVER INCLUDES EQUALITY HERE"@en ; cd:body "- The complementary claim: **≠, > or <**\n- Amoxicillin: mean **strictly above** the limit\n- Reject H₀ with sufficient evidence; non-rejection is **not proof**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-df-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Degrees of freedom: ν (nu)"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-df-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-df-a, ex:l6-df-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-df-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "SAMPLE SD: ONE FITTED MEAN"@en ; cd:body "- Estimate **one mean from the same observations**.\n- Residuals then **add to zero**: one fitted constraint.\n- Residual **degrees of freedom ν = n − 1**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-df-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "CALIBRATION LINE: TWO FITTED COEFFICIENTS"@en ; cd:body "- Fit **intercept and slope** to the same observations.\n- Two independent fitted coefficients leave **ν = n − 2**.\n- For these full-rank models, **each fitted coefficient costs one residual degree of freedom**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-p-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "The p-value: how unusual is our result if H₀ holds?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-p-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-p-a, ex:l6-p-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-p-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "ONE PROBABILITY SCALE FOR DIFFERENT TESTS"@en ; cd:body "- Assume H₀ and the test's sampling model\n- Count results **at least as extreme as ours**\n- Their probability is the p-value: the shaded tail area."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-p-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "COMPARE p WITH THE ALPHA CHOSEN BEFOREHAND"@en ; cd:body "- **p at or below alpha:** reject H₀ in favour of H₁\n- **p above alpha:** do not reject H₀\n- Small p challenges H₀; it does **not** give the probability that H₀ is true."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-p-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "The planned direction determines which t-reference tail is counted"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "The t-test compares means"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-t-a, ex:l6-t-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "ONE MEAN AGAINST A FIXED VALUE"@en ; cd:body "- A common test for a population mean\n- Example: QC mean **48.5 µg/L** against target **50 µg/L**\n- Also possible: compare a mean with a specified limit."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "TWO MEANS AGAINST EACH OTHER"@en ; cd:body "- Both group means are estimated\n- Diclofenac **before / after the industrial park**: upstream / downstream\n- The appropriate version depends on the sampling design."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-one-t-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "One-sample t-test: compare the mean with the target"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-crm-answer-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Can we demonstrate mean recovery above the 80% minimum?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-crm-answer a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-crm-a, ex:l6-crm-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-crm-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "WORKED RESULT"@en ; cd:body "For **101, 100, 102, 103, 101, 102%**, the mean is 101.5% and sample SD is 1.049 percentage points. The statistic is **t = 3.503**, df = 5; the two-sided p-value is **0.0172**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-crm-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "INTERPRETATION"@en ; cd:body "At a prespecified 5% two-sided level, reject the fixed 100% mean model under independent Normal preparation errors. The estimated departure is **+1.5 percentage points**. Assess its practical size and the reference uncertainty separately. Synthetic teaching case."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-pooled-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Pooled t-test: independent groups, one variance"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-paired-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Paired t-test: before and after batch oxidation"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-paired-answer a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-paired-a, ex:l6-paired-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-paired-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "SAME SITES, TWO OCCASIONS"@en ; cd:body "Before: **12, 18, 9, 21, 15, 25 mg/L**. After: **10, 15, 9, 17, 12, 20 mg/L** in the same site order. Before-minus-after differences: **2, 3, 0, 4, 3, 5 mg/L**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-paired-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "MEAN PAIRED CHANGE"@en ; cd:body "Mean difference **2.833 mg/L**, difference SD 1.722 mg/L; t = **4.029**, df = 5, two-sided p = **0.0100**. The model supports a positive mean before-minus-after change across represented sites. A causal treatment claim additionally needs an appropriate design. Synthetic data."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-welch-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Welch t-test: NIR sensor versus HPLC-MS"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-welch-case a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-welch-a, ex:l6-welch-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-welch-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "INDEPENDENT EXPOSURE VESSELS"@en ; cd:body "Response, a.u.: control **8, 9, 10, 11, 12**; exposure **10, 12, 14, 16, 18, 20**. One value per independently randomized vessel. Group means are **10 and 15 a.u.**; sample sizes are 5 and 6."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-welch-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "DIRECTION AND UNCERTAINTY"@en ; cd:body "Control-minus-exposure is **−5 a.u.** Welch gives t = **−2.970**, df ≈ **6.972**, two-sided p ≈ **0.0209**. Report the higher exposure-group response with its interval and assay meaning. The constructed response alone does not establish a toxicity mechanism."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-cascade-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Which test comes next? Plan before looking at p"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cascade a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-cascade-a, ex:l6-cascade-b, ex:l6-cascade-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cascade-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "1 · CHOOSE FROM THE STUDY DESIGN"@en ; cd:body "- Same sites twice? **Paired test.**\n- Separate groups? Usually **Welch**.\n- A non-significant variance test does not prove equal spread."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cascade-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "2 · COUNT THE QUESTIONS"@en ; cd:body "- Growth, reproduction, enzyme response: **three claims**.\n- Call the planned set a **family**.\n- Choose its error rule **before seeing p-values**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cascade-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "3 · PLAN THE FOLLOW-UPS"@en ; cd:body "- Coming later: **ANOVA** asks whether any group mean differs.\n- Pairwise tests ask **which groups** differ.\n- First, learn how Bonferroni protects the planned family."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-bonferroni-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Bonferroni: protect all three below-limit claims"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Next question: what can a ratio of scatter tell us?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-f-a, ex:l6-f-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "DOES METHOD A SCATTER MORE?"@en ; cd:body "- Repeat the same measurement with methods A and B.\n- Compare their **estimated variances**.\n- The exact F test needs independent Normal samples; non-Normal data can mislead it."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "DOES A MODEL EXPLAIN MORE?"@en ; cd:body "- Compare group differences with scatter inside groups.\n- Or ask whether adding a calibration term helps.\n- Both can use F, but **the two quantities being divided differ**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-ratio-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Method A has twice the SD: is that convincing?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-special-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Can one calibration dataset give an F-test?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-special a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-f-special-a, ex:l6-f-special-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-special-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "YES · COMPARE TWO FITS"@en ; cd:body "- Fit a flat line, then add a concentration slope.\n- Both fits use **the same observations**.\n- For one added term, F is the squared coefficient t statistic under the same Normal-error model. It tests either slope direction."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-special-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "NOT THE SAME AS ONE VARIANCE"@en ; cd:body "- Sample variance versus **known target variance**: chi-square.\n- Sample variance versus **another estimated variance**: F.\n- Ask where the comparison value came from."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-nested-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Does a curved calibration fit better than a straight line?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-nested-case a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-nested-a, ex:l6-nested-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-nested-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "SAME TEN STANDARDS"@en ; cd:body "- Straight line: **2 fitted coefficients**.\n- Add one curve term: **3 fitted coefficients**.\n- Sum of squared errors falls from **12 to 5**. Synthetic summaries."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-nested-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "IS THE GAIN LARGE ENOUGH?"@en ; cd:body "- Gain: **7** for one extra coefficient.\n- Remaining error per df: **5/7**.\n- **F = 9.8**, df (1, 7); use the upper tail. Also inspect remaining errors and the working range."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-anova-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "ANOVA: do all three exposure groups have the same mean?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-anova-case a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-anova-a, ex:l6-anova-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-anova-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "THREE EXPOSURE GROUPS"@en ; cd:body "Independent vessel responses: **4, 5, 6**; **7, 8, 9**; **10, 11, 12 a.u.** Group means are 5, 8 and 11 a.u. Between-group SS is 54 and within-group SS is 6, both in squared a.u."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-anova-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "JOINT RESULT"@en ; cd:body "With df **(2, 6)**, the mean squares are 27 and 1, so **F = 27**, p = **0.001**. Under independent common-variance Normal errors, reject equality of all population means. Planned adjusted contrasts identify the supported differences. Synthetic teaching data."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-chi-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Chi-square: are we comparing spread or counting things?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-chi-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-chi-a, ex:l6-chi-b, ex:l6-chi-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-chi-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "1 · TOO MUCH MEASUREMENT SCATTER?"@en ; cd:body "- Compare a sample variance with a **known target**.\n- Exact for independent results from one **Normal population**.\n- Input: **numeric measurements**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-chi-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "2 · THE EXPECTED PARTICLE MIX?"@en ; cd:body "- Count particles in each category.\n- Compare with **predicted counts**.\n- Approximate reference: check expected counts and fitted parameters."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-chi-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "3 · DOES EXPOSURE RELATE TO DAMAGE?"@en ; cd:body "- Count affected / unaffected vessels in each group.\n- One independent vessel enters one cell.\n- Small expected counts? Consider an exact test or simulation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-variance-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Is measurement scatter above the known target?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-pearson-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Do the particle counts match the expected mix?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-independence-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Is exposure group associated with damage?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-mw-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Mann–Whitney: are values in one group usually higher?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-mw-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-mw-a, ex:l6-mw-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-mw-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "BACK TO NUMERIC VALUES · COMPARE ORDER"@en ; cd:body "- Separate groups **X and Y**: compare every X with every Y.\n- Count **higher, tied or lower**.\n- **H₀: equal distributions**; group labels are exchangeable."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-mw-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "WHAT DOES THE RESULT MEAN?"@en ; cd:body "- Assess **distributional differences** through ordering.\n- A median-shift reading needs **same-shaped distributions**.\n- Below-detection-limit values require methods that **account for the detection limit**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-u-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Mann–Whitney U: count wins and give ties half credit"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-signed-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Wilcoxon signed ranks: do paired measurements show a shift?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-signed-case a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-signed-a, ex:l6-signed-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-signed-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "FIVE SITE CHANGES"@en ; cd:body "- Synthetic differences: **1, −2, 3, 4, 5 µg/L**.\n- Rank absolute sizes; then restore the signs.\n- Positive ranks total **13**; negative ranks total **2**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-signed-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "FOUR POSITIVE SIGNS ARE NOT ENOUGH"@en ; cd:body "- Exact two-sided **p = 0.1875** from 32 sign assignments.\n- At 5%: **do not reject** zero shift.\n- Shift inference needs independent, symmetric differences. A sign test ignores sizes; ties/zeros need a stated rule."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Power: would we detect a difference that really exists?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-power-a, ex:l6-power-b, ex:l6-power-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "WHAT SHOULD WE BE ABLE TO FIND?"@en ; cd:body "- Choose a scientifically useful difference.\n- Estimate plausible spread; explore several values.\n- Plan the test, alpha, direction and independent sample size."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "HOW CAN WE SEE IT MORE CLEARLY?"@en ; cd:body "- More independent vessels can increase power.\n- Less measurement noise can help.\n- Measuring one vessel four times does **not** create four independent vessels."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "WHAT DO WE REPORT AFTERWARDS?"@en ; cd:body "- Report the estimated difference and its interval.\n- Do not turn observed-effect power into a second result.\n- Power is **not** the probability that H₁ is true."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-effect-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Cohen's d: mean difference relative to within-group spread"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-effect-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-effect-a, ex:l6-effect-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-effect-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "START WITH THE CHANGE AND ITS INTERVAL"@en ; cd:body "- River mean decrease: **2.833 mg/L**.\n- **95% confidence interval: 1.026 to 4.641 mg/L**; paired t, no multiplicity adjustment.\n- Compatible mean changes are positive, but are they important? A small p alone cannot answer."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-effect-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "IF DIVIDING BY AN SD, NAME IT"@en ; cd:body "- Independent-group Cohen's d: **pooled group SD**.\n- Paired d_z: **SD of pair differences**.\n- Hedges' g corrects small-sample bias in a chosen d. Report the correction and an uncertainty interval."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Cliff's delta: which group tends to have larger values?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff-case a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-cliff-a, ex:l6-cliff-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "REUSE OUR NINE COMPARISONS"@en ; cd:body "- X: **1, 2, 2**; Y: **2, 3, 4 a.u.**\n- X wins **0**, loses **7**, ties **2**.\n- Delta: **−7/9 ≈ −0.778**; U for X is **1**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "READ THE SIGN, THEN THE SIZE"@en ; cd:body "- Negative here: **X tends to be smaller than Y**.\n- Ties still count in the total.\n- Nine comparisons reuse six observations: estimate uncertainty from the original independent units, not nine independent pairs."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-outlier-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Grubbs outlier test: mistake or real nitrate event?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-outlier-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-outlier-a, ex:l6-outlier-b, ex:l6-outlier-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-outlier-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "1 · KEEP ALL SIX NITRATE RESULTS"@en ; cd:body "- **9.8, 9.9, 10.0, 10.1, 10.2, 12.5 mg/L**.\n- Keep **12.5** and its original sample ID.\n- A high result can be a real pollution pulse."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-outlier-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "2 · CHECK WHAT THE TEST ASSUMES"@en ; cd:body "- Grubbs checks **one suspect extreme**.\n- Other results: independent Normal background.\n- Several extremes can hide each other. Never delete and retest blindly."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-outlier-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "3 · INVESTIGATE, THEN REPORT"@en ; cd:body "- Check blanks, preparation and instrument records.\n- A flag is **not permission to delete**.\n- Explain exclusions; compare with the original data retained."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Grubbs: how far is 12.5 mg/L from the other results?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-critical-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Grubbs: why not use an ordinary t cutoff?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-case a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-grubbs-a, ex:l6-grubbs-b ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "SIX PREPARATIONS"@en ; cd:body "Synthetic nitrate results **9.8, 9.9, 10.0, 10.1, 10.2, 12.5 mg/L** have mean 10.4167 mg/L and sample SD 1.0304 mg/L. The two-sided Grubbs statistic is **2.0219**; its 5% critical value is **1.8871**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "FLAG, INVESTIGATE, REPORT"@en ; cd:body "The selected maximum exceeds the single-outlier Normal-model cutoff. **Flag 12.5 mg/L for investigation**. Keep its identity and review preparation and measurement records before deciding how the result enters a reported estimate."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-report-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Report the change, uncertainty and limits"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-report a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-report-a, ex:l6-report-b, ex:l6-report-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-report-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "WHAT DID WE COMPARE?"@en ; cd:body "- Synthetic concentration: **six independent sites, two times**.\n- **Before minus after**; all six differences retained.\n- One planned contrast; **no multiplicity adjustment**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-report-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "HOW DID WE TEST IT?"@en ; cd:body "- **Paired t = 4.029, df 5; two-sided p = 0.0100**.\n- Independent Normal differences; prespecified **alpha 5%**.\n- Reject zero population mean change."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-report-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "WHAT DOES IT MEAN?"@en ; cd:body "- Mean decrease: **2.833 mg/L**.\n- **95% confidence interval: 1.026 to 4.641 mg/L**.\n- Relevance needs a justified threshold; cause remains unknown."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
